# The vendored copy of svfrontend/src/types/content.ts is compared BYTE FOR BYTE
# by `npm run check:drift`. svfrontend normalises to LF via its own
# .gitattributes; this repo has no such rule, so with core.autocrlf=true every
# Windows checkout rewrote this file to CRLF and the byte comparison could never
# match. Pinning it to LF makes the two working copies identical on any platform.
src/types/frontend-contract.ts text eol=lf

# The blog contract is vendored and byte-compared the same way, from
# svfrontend/src/types/blog.ts. It needs the identical pin for the identical
# reason — see above. The frontend keeps the blog in its OWN file so that
# "adding the blog cannot destabilise the project and site-settings reads", and
# mirroring that split here is what lets the blog gain a checked contract
# without touching the existing byte-identical one.
src/types/frontend-contract-blog.ts text eol=lf

# The hero-media contract, vendored from svfrontend/src/types/heroMedia.ts and
# byte-compared the same way. Same pin, same reason.
src/types/frontend-contract-hero.ts text eol=lf

# The project-video contract, vendored from svfrontend/src/types/projectMedia.ts
# and byte-compared the same way. Same pin, same reason.
src/types/frontend-contract-project-media.ts text eol=lf
